Hi Michael,

Brandon and I reconciled the costs yesterday using the same normal month of 1=
00,000 original records for both conditions. The second-read proposal comes t=
o USD 4,800 per month, USD 300 over the USD 4,500 application ceiling; the op=
ening-only estimate is USD 3,600. The increase is USD 1,000 for the accelerat=
or and USD 200 for the host.

We are holding the proposed route for use and continuing the current human ch=
ecking. The research comparison remains useful: the 32 and 24 misses are out =
of the same 1,000 action-required records in the independent 4,000-record eva=
luation. Fourteen misses were recovered, but six records became new misses un=
der the proposal.

I've attached the use decision and Brandon's itemized monthly calculation sep=
arately. Before reconsidering use, we need a cost measurement within the ceil=
ing at the applicable workload, evidence on peak response, and clarity on who=
 would recover misrouted records and the work involved. Brandon and I will br=
ing the arrival and review-path questions together by August 25.

Thanks,
Vanessa


